[gd_scene load_steps=7 format=3 uid="uid://wardbfixpillcup01"]

; Paper medication cup with a single pill resting inside — Room 1's "take
; the pill", the first interactable in the game, so it must read as obvious
; and inviting on a dark table. Cup wall is one CylinderMesh with
; cap_top = false, cap_bottom = true: Godot's per-cap toggle does in one
; mesh what world.ts's buildPillCup needed two meshes for (an open-ended
; CylinderGeometry plus a separate CircleGeometry base). Capsule is the same
; two-tone construction as pill_pickup.tscn (cylinder body + two hemisphere
; caps), scaled down and reused per world.ts's buildCapsuleMesh comment
; ("shared across pill_pickup/pill_cup instances").
;
; Canonical frame: width +X, height +Y, depth +Z, front faces -Z, origin at
; the centre of the 0.18 x 0.22 x 0.18 fixture volume.
;
; Idle motion (pill_idle.gd) is dialed down from pill_pickup's: a spinning
; paper cup on a table reads as a bug, not a hint, so spin/bob are subtle
; here while the emissive pulse stays at full strength — the glow, not the
; motion, is what has to carry readability for a gameplay-critical pickup.

